:: "Chute system?" {"position":"800,1375","size":"100,100"}
Oh yes, marvellous invention, that. It transports from one room to another in the blink of an eye. Makes giving items to guests much more efficient. To use it, simply place an item inside, and then select a chute on this computer. Any questions?

[["Yes"]]
[["No"]]
[["How much am I getting paid?"]]


:: "Derek" {"position":"675,750","size":"100,100"}
Derek, eh? Well, for all intensive purposes, let's call you Steve from here on.

[["Alright"]] 
[["Why?"]] 


:: "Happiness Supervisor?" {"position":"800,1000","size":"100,100"}
Oh yes, Happiness Supervisor. It’s a new job title I invented, ‘Random Task Doer’ wasn’t really getting that many applicants.

[["I thought I was just a security guard"]]


:: "How do I send the item to Room 7?" {"position":"675,1625","size":"100,100"}
Manager: Well, it’s quite simple, really, you can see on the camera feed where the chute you need to send it to is, so just do that

[["The camera doesn't show the room number"]]


:: "How much am I getting paid?" {"position":"800,1625","size":"100,100"}
Splendid, then let's get started.
Now, your task. One of our guests here in Room 7 has requested for some quiche to be delivered via our-state-of-the-art chute system. There should already be one somewhere in your office, so get to it.

[["How do I send the item to Room 7?"]]



:: "I still can't figure it out" {"position":"675,1875","size":"100,100"}
*sigh* Ok, do you see the room layouts on the blueprint? Each layout is unique, so you should be able to work out which room on the cameras is which from there. Once you’ve done that, it should be clear.



:: "I thought I was just a security guard" {"position":"800,1125","size":"100,100"}
Yes, we employ that trick too, gets even more people signing up. Your job is basically to do whatever it takes by any means necessary to keep our clients happy. If they’re dissatisfied, it won’t look good for you.

[["Right..."]]


